{
  "case_id": "2007-06-984",
  "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2d9545532c-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2d9545532c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The President and the Senate entered into three treaties, the Optional Protocol, the UN Charter, and the ICJ Statute, by which the United States agreed that it would comply with the ICJ's decision in any case to which it was a party."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2d9545532c-0000-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose, for example, that the International Court of Justice determined in this case its judgment was the same, but they added: As a matter of deterrence, we think the officers who failed to give consular warning should each be sentenced to 5 years in jail."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2d9545532c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Does the ICJ ever issue a judgment of that character?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2d9545532c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: And can the President displace our authority to do that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Donovan",
      "case_id": "2007-06-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2d9545532c-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DONOVAN: The President would not displace the Court's authority to interpret a judgment, no. What the President has said is that the judgment shall be enforced. That's an independent source of Federal law under his Article II --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Donovan",
      "case_id": "2007-06-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2d9545532c-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DONOVAN: You have two separate and independent sources of authority here. Without the President's determination, this Court pursuant to the mandate in the Supremacy Clause would apply the treaty obligation to comply with the judgment because the nature of the judgment is such to be enforced in a court of justice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2d9545532c-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: We would have no -- according to you, we would have no obligation to enforce this judgment but for the President's action?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2007-06-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2d9545532c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The entirety of the United States's argument is predicated on the idea that the President's two-paragraph memorandum is in and of itself binding Federal law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2007-06-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2d9545532c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the United States strenuously disagrees with that proposition. And, indeed, the United States explicitly disclaims these treaties as the source of his authority; in fact, expressly agrees with this Court's decision in Sanchez-Llamas."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2d9545532c-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Suppose you have a judge who has control over a defendant who's being held in custody pending trial, and the defendant says I want to see my -- my foreign counsel. The judge says no. Can you mandate that -- assuming State procedures allow him in, couldn't you mandate that judge to require him to allow the notification to take place?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cruz",
      "case_id": "2007-06-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2d9545532c-0004-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The United States believes that the President has the authority to make decisions and to implement treaties -- an independent authority to create new binding law, even though the obligation is not self-executing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2d9545532c-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 77,
        "start": 77
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And has any other State acted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-984",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe2d9545532c5a621c63ae9eefa8f0a501f5eeb881702098cfc64b82ecea85b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe2d9545532c-0004-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
